// Erebus Strait: two against two across a polar sea. Each team holds one
// coast of Antarctica under its ice sheet, mountains between its two starts;
// two volcanic islands with flooded calderas lie in the strait, tabular bergs
// aground round them; thick sea ice along the coasts and round the islands,
// open water down the strait between. Nothing grows. A grey, windy day: a
// dark, rough sea, cloud low over the ice, snow showers blowing through.
// Skirmish set-up can override the weather (Stormy for a blizzard) and the
// time of day.
(
    style: Teams,
    weather: Cloudy,
    tweaks: (rain: 0.75, wind: 18, mist: 0.3, towering: 0.4),
    time: Morning,
    climate: Polar,
)
